+/// handler when it has one of the forms above. The generic handler stays for everything else.
+/// The specialised handlers (except LDM/STM) do not check whether the block ends after them, so
+/// this leaves out the last instruction of a page (a block ends there) and must not be used for
+/// single-step translations.
+void SpecializeArmInstruction(arm_inst* inst_base, u32 inst, u32 pc);
